# no-cli-model-providers.allow — data file for scripts/check-no-cli-model-providers.sh
#
# Files that MAY still name the CLI-backed model providers deleted by WU-24
# (founder 2026-10-14). Everything NOT listed here must be clean.
#
# Why these and only these: they are historical decision records — ADRs, dated
# internal specs, their review and task reports, and one dated research note —
# that mention the retired kinds AS HISTORY. Rewriting a past decision's text
# to erase a name is falsifying the record, not removing a trace (same ruling
# as ADR-068 §2.4 for its own deletions, and the same mechanism as
# scripts/no-removed-providers.allow).
#
# Format: one path per line, relative to the repo root, POSIX extended regular
# expression anchored at both ends by the guard. Blank lines and `#` comments
# are ignored. Keep this list SHORT — every row here is a hole in the guard.
# Never add live product code, user docs, or a new design document here: a
# NEW document naming the retired kinds is a finding, not history.

# --- this allow-list itself -------------------------------------------------
scripts/no-cli-model-providers\.allow

# --- ADRs: the decisions that built (and partly retired) these providers ----
docs/internal/architecture/ADR-019-v01-workspaces-foundation(-review)?\.md
docs/internal/architecture/ADR-031-connectors-providers-redesign(-review)?\.md
docs/internal/architecture/ADR-053-bedrock-provider-first-class\.md
docs/internal/architecture/ADR-066-[^/]*\.md
